💭 Byte-oriented string helpers. 🔍 returns byte offsets, so slicing has to be
💭 byte-based too (🔪 on 🔡 slices graphemes and would drift on non-ASCII input).
🌍 🐇 🧰 🍇
  📗 Substring by byte offset and byte length. 📗
  🐇❗️ ✂️ s 🔡 from 🔢 length 🔢 ➡️ 🔡 🍇
    ↪️ length ◀️🙌 0 🍇
      ↩️ 🔤🔤
    🍉
    ↪️ 🔡 🔪 📇 s❗️ from length❗️❗️ ➡️ out 🍇
      ↩️ out
    🍉
    ↩️ 🔤🔤
  🍉

  📗 Everything after the first *skip* bytes. 📗
  🐇❗️ 🦶 s 🔡 skip 🔢 ➡️ 🔡 🍇
    ↩️ ✂️🐇🧰 s skip 📐 s❗️ ➖ skip❗️
  🍉

  📗 Split on the first occurrence of *sep*. Returns one or two parts. 📗
  🐇❗️ ✌️ s 🔡 sep 🔡 ➡️ 🍨🐚🔡🍆 🍇
    ↪️ 🔍 s sep❗️ ➡️ index 🍇
      ↩️ 🍿 ✂️🐇🧰 s 0 index❗️ 🦶🐇🧰 s index ➕ 📐 sep❗️❗️ 🍆
    🍉
    ↩️ 🍿 s 🍆
  🍉

  📗 Replace every occurrence of *find* with *with*. 📗
  🐇❗️ 🔄 s 🔡 find 🔡 with 🔡 ➡️ 🔡 🍇
    ↩️ 🆕🔡 🔫 s find❗️ with❗️
  🍉

  📗 Whether *b* is ASCII whitespace (space, tab, CR, LF). 📗
  🐇❗️ 💨 b 💧 ➡️ 👌 🍇
    ↩️ b 🙌 32 👐 b 🙌 9 👐 b 🙌 10 👐 b 🙌 13
